{
  "verdict": "pended",
  "governing_rule": "MP-ORT-001",
  "reason": "Member is eligible, the provider is in-network and in the plan's service area, benefit accumulators have adequate remaining balance, and the submitted diagnosis (M17.11) supports the requested procedure (CPT 27447, total knee arthroplasty). However, the clinical documentation submitted does not address key medical policy criteria: there is no report of weight-bearing radiographs establishing Kellgren-Lawrence grade 3/4 changes, no documentation of a trial of conservative management (physical therapy, medication, injections, assistive device, etc.) over at least three months, and no documentation of preoperative medical evaluation/surgical candidacy assessment. Functional limitation (Criterion 3) is adequately documented, but the remaining criteria are unaddressed. Additional records are needed before a medical necessity determination can be made.",
  "missing_information": [
    "Weight-bearing radiographs of the right knee (within 12 months) with Kellgren-Lawrence grade documented",
    "Documentation of at least 3 months of conservative management (e.g., physical therapy, NSAID/analgesic course, intra-articular injections, assistive device use) with duration and outcome of each modality",
    "Documentation of preoperative medical evaluation confirming surgical candidacy, including consideration of comorbidities affecting operative risk"
  ]
}
